# Tapua'i documentation engine

Do not ship code that leaves JSDoc or system docs stale. Project continuity depends on this.

## 0. `docs/STATE.md` is the entry point — read it first, update it last

`docs/STATE.md` is what every agent and engineer reads before touching the repo: current state,
what changed most recently, environment gotchas, and the list of knowingly-broken things.

**Any change under `apps/`, `packages/` or `supabase/` must add a line to `docs/STATE.md` §4 and
bump its `Last updated` header, in the same turn as the code.** CI fails pull requests that do
not. Keep §4 to ~15 entries, newest first; older history belongs in `CHANGELOG.md`.

**Synchronization specialist:** Dispatch `DOCUMENTATION` for changes spanning teams or user journeys. Each feature owner supplies changed files/APIs and actual verification evidence. The update agent synchronizes affected documents and definitions; preserve generated fact blocks and approved legal conclusions.

**Execution receipt:** The lead records the actual Documentation executor/session, affected
files, check result/date, remaining gaps and next owner in the existing task tracker. Assign
`VP_OPERATIONS` when roles, protocols or priorities change and retain its reconciliation receipt.
Root integrates shared status and releases claims after checks. A required correction still
open means the handoff is not complete. Available role files do not start background workers;
name the actual outside-session runtime when one performs the function. Current checkpoint:
`docs/agents/COORD-01.md`.

## 1. Comments: every file has a header; JSDoc on hooks, API calls, and complex components

**IP-01 upkeep:** On source/dependency/asset/contributor/disclosure changes, DOCUMENTATION and
source owners update factual candidates/rights gaps in `docs/legal/ip-register.json`, then run
`pnpm ip:sync` / `pnpm ip:check`. Read `docs/legal/IP_PROTECTION_PLAN.md`; preserve reviews
and supplied decisions. Hashes cannot infer inventions/ownership or renew stale reviews.
LEGAL coordinates counsel; owner approves sharing/spend/filings. Record actual checks in IP-01.
Local full checks refresh facts; no idle paid AI worker or automatic filing is established.

Every source file under `apps/mobile/app` and `apps/mobile/src` starts with a short header comment (what it is,
where it fits, what it touches). `pnpm comments:check` enforces it in CI. Inline comments explain *why*, not
*what*. Full rules: `docs/engineering/CONVENTIONS.md` §5.

Add a TSDoc/JSDoc header on:

- Every **custom hook** (`useTipCheckout`, `useLiveScores`, new hooks, etc.)
- Every **API / RPC / Stripe / Storage** helper that talks to the network
- Every **complex component** (multi-step UI, Realtime, PaymentSheet, Aura chrome, operator console)

```
/**
 * @purpose What this does in product language (Donate, Seki, Aura, operator clock).
 * @param name Description of each input.
 * @returns Description of the return value or rendered UI.
 * @sideEffects Supabase queries, Realtime channels, Stripe, Storage, AsyncStorage, haptics.
 */
```

- Omit `@sideEffects` only when there are none.
- Skip one-liner formatters unless they encode business rules (e.g. Aura point math).
- UI copy: **Donate / donation** (docs/product/VOICE.md), **Seki**. Persistence keeps the code names: `tips` / `useTipCheckout`.

## 2. Schema or architecture changes MUST sync docs in the same turn

If you change tables, RLS, RPCs, Storage, Aura tiers, routing, env vars, payments, Realtime, or phase status, you **must** update:

| If you change… | You also update… |
| --- | --- |
| **Anything under `apps/` / `packages/` / `supabase/`** | **`docs/STATE.md` §4 + `Last updated`** |
| Who owns a screen, or what a department does now / next / later | **`docs/agents/TEAMS.md`** business row + squad section, and `.claude/agents/<file>.md`, `registry.json`, and `docs/agents/TEAM_HIERARCHY.md`; run `pnpm agents:check` |
| Terms, minors, the donation split, footage rights, or school marks | **`docs/agents/TEAMS.md`** Legal team table. Do not write a new legal conclusion. |
| Architecture, folders, roadmap | `docs/engineering/SYSTEM_OVERVIEW.md` · `docs/engineering/ARCHITECTURE.md` |
| Tables, FKs, RLS, RPCs, palette, buckets | `docs/engineering/SCHEMA.md` |
| Clone / env / Metro / Expo Go | `docs/ONBOARDING.md` |
| Folder law | `AGENTS.md` |
| Landed feature or schema | `CHANGELOG.md` |
| Mālo / exclusive / booster prices, Aura math, operator PIN, Connect identity, admin platform cuts | `pnpm docs:sync` (PUBLIC / INVESTOR / LEGAL fact blocks) |
| Athlete sports, class years, team catalog badges | `pnpm docs:sync` + `docs/engineering/SCHEMA.md` (`schools_and_teams`) |
| Highlight / Highlights ⚡ copy, profile tabs (Highlights / Stats / Vault), Spotlight fan-bar label | `pnpm docs:sync` (`HIGHLIGHT_*` / `SPOTLIGHT_NAV_LABEL` in `highlights.ts`) |
| Athlete Vault lock / Open Vault copy | `pnpm docs:sync` (`VAULT_LOCK_ACTION` / `VAULT_OPEN_ACTION`) |

Prompt yourself: “Did schema or architecture move? Then `docs/engineering/SYSTEM_OVERVIEW.md` + `docs/engineering/SCHEMA.md` are part of this diff.”

Aliases to keep honest:

- `video_tips` → `public.tips` (+ `reels.total_tips_cents`)
- `add_user_aura(user_id, points)` → `add_user_aura(target_user_id, points_to_add)`
- Changing `get_aura_tier` return type requires `DROP FUNCTION` first

## 3. Required suite (never delete)

0. `docs/STATE.md` — current state, recent changes, known breakage, open decisions.
1. `docs/engineering/SYSTEM_OVERVIEW.md` — mission, Expo + Supabase + Stripe test mode, directory map, Phase 1/2/3.
2. `docs/engineering/ARCHITECTURE.md` — monorepo map (mobile / admin-portal / shared-types).
3. `docs/engineering/SCHEMA.md` — `profiles`, `reels`, `games`, video tips, RPCs, 7-tier palette, RLS, `game_highlights`.
4. `docs/ONBOARDING.md` — clone, `pnpm install`, `apps/mobile/.env.local`, `pnpm mobile`.

## 4. Front-of-house memos (same turn)

If you change Mālo amounts, exclusive price, booster dollars, Aura math/tiers, operator PIN, Connect identity, custodial payout copy, parent consent, demo RLS language, Vault lock / Open Vault copy, or admin platform cuts:

1. Run `pnpm docs:sync` (writes `docs/product/PRODUCT_FACTS.md` and the `<!-- product-facts -->` blocks in `docs/product/PUBLIC.md`, `docs/company/INVESTOR.md`, `docs/legal/LEGAL_BRIEFING.md`).
2. Do **not** rewrite legal conclusions outside those markers.
3. If prices or prototype caveats change, update the investor canvas (`tapuai-investor-briefing`) when it is open.
4. If Reel / Local / Profile chrome changes and Expo is running, recapture `docs/company/press/*.png`. Otherwise mark STALE in `docs/company/press/README.md`.

`pnpm docs:check` also fails when `docs/engineering/SCHEMA.md` does not name every `public` table or `create or replace function` from `apps/mobile/src/backend/db/schema.sql`. New SQL must land in SCHEMA in the same turn.
